---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Sources from '../components/Sources.astro';
import RelatedTopics from '../components/RelatedTopics.astro';
import VerifiedDate from '../components/VerifiedDate.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Tech Stack Fundamentals"
  description="The tech stack knowledge every full-stack and AI-app developer needs: three jobs — ask, decide, store — done by whichever tools you picked. Drive a real browser, terminal, and database client, side by side, and watch one request move through all three."
>
  <p class="eyebrow"><a href="/systems/">← Systems</a></p>
  <h1>Tech Stack Fundamentals</h1>
  <VerifiedDate />

  <div class="workspace-page">
    <div class="workspace-shell">
      <aside class="docs-panel">
        <section class="docs-block">
          <p class="docs-label">TL;DR</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Three unchanging jobs: <strong>ask</strong> (frontend), <strong>decide</strong> (backend), <strong>store</strong> (database).</li>
            <li>MERN, LAMP, whatever's next — just names for which tool got picked per job.</li>
            <li>Name which layer a bug lives in, and any new framework gets faster to pick up.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section class="docs-block">
          <p class="docs-label">ELI5</p>
          <ul>
            <li>You tell the waiter what you want → <strong>frontend</strong>.</li>
            <li>The waiter decides what to do and passes it along → <strong>backend</strong>.</li>
            <li>The kitchen does the real work → <strong>database</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Swap any of the three — the jobs never change.</strong></li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section class="docs-block">
          <p class="docs-label">Technical definition</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Formally a <strong>three-tier architecture</strong>: presentation, application logic, and data persistence, each independently replaceable.</li>
            <li>Layers talk only over defined protocols — HTTP browser↔server, a query language server↔database — never by reaching into each other's internals.</li>
            <li>This lab models exactly that: three tiers, two protocols, one request.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section class="docs-block">
          <p class="docs-label">Real-world tools</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Frontend:</strong> React, Vue, Svelte — runs in the visitor's browser.</li>
            <li><strong>Backend:</strong> Node/Express, Django, Rails, Spring — runs on a server you control.</li>
            <li><strong>Database:</strong> PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB — where the real data actually lives.</li>
            <li>Same 3 jobs no matter which row you pick from each column.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section class="docs-block">
          <p class="docs-label">Why it matters</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Most bugs live at the <strong>seams</strong> between layers, not inside one.</li>
            <li>Security boundaries live at the server, never the browser — try <code>/login</code> in the workspace.</li>
            <li>Separation lets you swap one layer without rewriting the rest.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section class="docs-block">
          <p class="docs-label">Under the hood</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Stateless backend → can run 10 identical copies behind a load balancer.</li>
            <li>A database holds the one real copy, so it scales differently (replication, sharding) — not just "add more copies."</li>
            <li>Real stacks usually insert a <strong>cache</strong> (Redis, etc.) between server and database — skipped here on purpose to keep the 3 jobs clear.</li>
            <li>Routing is matching, not magic: this lab's "route table" is one regex; real frameworks do the same thing with more patterns.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section class="docs-block">
          <p class="docs-label">Failure modes</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>"Frontend hits the DB directly."</strong> Real stacks don't — the backend guards it.</li>
            <li><strong>"Error = frontend broken."</strong> Try user 99: the 404 starts at the database.</li>
            <li><strong>"More layers = worse."</strong> It's what lets a stack change one piece at a time.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section class="docs-block">
          <p class="docs-label">Where AI fits in</p>
          <ul>
            <li>An LLM call from your backend is just another outbound request — same job (decide), one more thing the server waits on before answering the browser.</li>
            <li>A <strong>vector database</strong> is still "store" — a specialized database tier for embeddings instead of rows, same job as the DB panel here.</li>
            <li>An agent loop or RAG pipeline adds steps, not new jobs — see <a href="/agentic-engineering/">Agentic Engineering</a> and <a href="/context-engineering/">Context Engineering</a> for what fills those extra steps.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </aside>

      <div class="workspace-main">
        <div class="workspace-toolbar">
          <span class="workspace-title">request-lifecycle.sim</span>
          <span class="workspace-hint">genuinely tiny router + in-memory DB — type any id, or a made-up path</span>
        </div>

        <div class="pipeline" role="img" aria-label="Browser connects to Server over HTTP; Server connects to Database over SQL">
          <div class="pipe-node" data-node="browser">
            <span class="pipe-icon" aria-hidden="true">▣</span>
            <span class="pipe-name">Browser</span>
            <span class="pipe-note">Sends the request, renders the result</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pipe-edge" data-edge="browser-server"><span class="pipe-edge-note">HTTP</span></div>
          <div class="pipe-node" data-node="server">
            <span class="pipe-icon" aria-hidden="true">▤</span>
            <span class="pipe-name">Server</span>
            <span class="pipe-note">Stateless — could run 10 identical copies</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pipe-edge" data-edge="server-database"><span class="pipe-edge-note">SQL</span></div>
          <div class="pipe-node" data-node="database">
            <span class="pipe-icon" aria-hidden="true">▦</span>
            <span class="pipe-name">Database</span>
            <span class="pipe-note">Holds the one real copy — scales differently</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="addr-input-row">
          <span class="addr-proto">GET https://example.app</span>
          <input id="path-input" class="addr-input" type="text" value="/api/users/2" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Request path" />
          <button type="button" id="go-btn" class="go-btn">Go ▶</button>
        </div>
        <div class="preset-chips">
          <button type="button" class="chip" data-path="/api/users/1">user 1</button>
          <button type="button" class="chip" data-path="/api/users/2">user 2</button>
          <button type="button" class="chip" data-path="/api/users/99">user 99 (missing)</button>
          <button type="button" class="chip" data-path="/login">/login (bad route)</button>
        </div>

        <div class="tool-grid">
          <div class="tool-window">
            <div class="tool-titlebar"><span class="tw-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="tw-tab">User Profile — browser</span></div>
            <div class="tool-body">
              <p class="net-log-label">Rendered page</p>
              <div class="rendered-page" id="rendered-page"><p class="rp-placeholder">Click Go or pick an example above.</p></div>
              <p class="net-log-label">Network</p>
              <div class="net-log" id="net-log" aria-live="polite"></div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="tool-window">
            <div class="tool-titlebar"><span class="tw-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="tw-tab">server.log — bash</span></div>
            <div class="tool-body terminal-body" id="log-server" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          </div>

          <div class="tool-window">
            <div class="tool-titlebar"><span class="tw-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="tw-tab">query — users</span></div>
            <div class="tool-body" aria-hidden="true">
              <p class="net-log-label">Query</p>
              <div class="query-line" id="db-query">— no query yet —</div>
              <p class="net-log-label">Results</p>
              <table class="db-table" id="db-table" hidden>
                <thead><tr><th>id</th><th>name</th><th>role</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody id="db-tbody"></tbody>
              </table>
              <p class="db-empty" id="db-empty" hidden>0 rows returned</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="footer-page">
    <RelatedTopics />

    <Sources
      sources={[
        {
          title: 'Client–server model — Wikipedia',
          url: 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Client%E2%80%93server_model',
          note: 'The foundational pattern every stack in this lab is built on.',
        },
        {
          title: 'Multitier architecture — Wikipedia',
          url: 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multitier_architecture',
          note: 'The formal name for splitting frontend, backend, and database into separate tiers.',
        },
        {
          title: 'HTTP overview — MDN Web Docs',
          url: 'https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Overview',
          note: 'The actual protocol the browser-to-server leg of this lab is modeling.',
        },
      ]}
    />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  import { scrambleText as decode } from '../lib/decode';
  import { handleRequest, type Layer } from '../lib/stack-sim';

  const input = document.getElementById('path-input') as HTMLInputElement;
  const goBtn = document.getElementById('go-btn') as HTMLButtonElement;
  const chips = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.chip');

  const nodes: Record<Layer, HTMLElement> = {
    browser: document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-node="browser"]')!,
    server: document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-node="server"]')!,
    database: document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-node="database"]')!,
  };
  const edges: Record<'browser-server' | 'server-database', HTMLElement> = {
    'browser-server': document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-edge="browser-server"]')!,
    'server-database': document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-edge="server-database"]')!,
  };

  const netLog = document.getElementById('net-log')!;
  const terminal = document.getElementById('log-server')!;
  const queryLine = document.getElementById('db-query')!;
  const dbTable = document.getElementById('db-table') as HTMLTableElement;
  const dbBody = document.getElementById('db-tbody')!;
  const dbEmpty = document.getElementById('db-empty')!;
  const renderedPage = document.getElementById('rendered-page')!;

  const LAYER_TAG: Record<Layer, string> = { browser: 'BR', server: 'SRV', database: 'DB' };

  let runTimer: number | undefined;

  function edgeKey(a: Layer, b: Layer): 'browser-server' | 'server-database' | undefined {
    const set = new Set([a, b]);
    if (set.has('browser') && set.has('server')) return 'browser-server';
    if (set.has('server') && set.has('database')) return 'server-database';
    return undefined;
  }

  function clearAll() {
    for (const el of Object.values(nodes)) el.classList.remove('active');
    for (const el of Object.values(edges)) el.classList.remove('active');
    netLog.innerHTML = '';
    terminal.innerHTML = '';
    queryLine.textContent = '— no query yet —';
    dbBody.innerHTML = '';
    dbEmpty.hidden = true;
    dbTable.hidden = true;
  }

  function renderOutcome(status: number, body: unknown) {
    renderedPage.innerHTML = '';
    if (status === 200 && body && typeof body === 'object') {
      const user = body as { id: number; name: string; role: string };
      const card = document.createElement('div');
      card.className = 'profile-card';
      const avatar = document.createElement('span');
      avatar.className = 'avatar';
      avatar.textContent = user.name.split(' ').map((w) => w[0]).join('');
      const name = document.createElement('span');
      name.className = 'p-name';
      name.textContent = user.name;
      const role = document.createElement('span');
      role.className = 'p-role';
      role.textContent = user.role;
      const id = document.createElement('span');
      id.className = 'p-id';
      id.textContent = `id: ${user.id}`;
      card.append(avatar, name, role, id);
      renderedPage.append(card);
    } else if (body && typeof body === 'object' && (body as { error?: string }).error === 'User not found') {
      const wrap = document.createElement('div');
      wrap.className = 'app-404';
      const glyph = document.createElement('span');
      glyph.className = 'app-404-glyph';
      glyph.textContent = '⌗';
      const p = document.createElement('p');
      p.textContent = 'User not found';
      wrap.append(glyph, p);
      renderedPage.append(wrap);
    } else {
      const wrap = document.createElement('div');
      wrap.className = 'browser-404';
      const glyph = document.createElement('span');
      glyph.className = 'browser-404-glyph';
      glyph.textContent = '✕';
      const p = document.createElement('p');
      p.textContent = "This page can't be found";
      wrap.append(glyph, p);
      renderedPage.append(wrap);
    }
  }

  function run(path: string) {
    if (runTimer) { clearTimeout(runTimer); runTimer = undefined; }
    clearAll();
    input.value = path;
    renderedPage.innerHTML = '<p class="rp-loading">loading…</p>';
    const result = handleRequest('GET', path);
    let seenDb = 0;
    let prevLayer: Layer | undefined;
    let i = 0;

    const step = () => {
      if (i >= result.log.length) {
        renderOutcome(result.status, result.body);
        return;
      }
      const entry = result.log[i];

      for (const el of Object.values(nodes)) el.classList.remove('active');
      for (const el of Object.values(edges)) el.classList.remove('active');
      nodes[entry.layer].classList.add('active');
      if (prevLayer && prevLayer !== entry.layer) {
        const key = edgeKey(prevLayer, entry.layer);
        if (key) edges[key].classList.add('active');
      }
      prevLayer = entry.layer;

      const line = document.createElement('p');
      line.className = 'sim-line';
      const tag = document.createElement('span');
      tag.className = `net-tag net-tag-${entry.layer}`;
      tag.textContent = LAYER_TAG[entry.layer];
      const textSpan = document.createElement('span');
      line.append(tag, document.createTextNode(' '), textSpan);
      netLog.append(line);
      netLog.scrollTop = netLog.scrollHeight;

      if (entry.layer === 'server') {
        const t = document.createElement('p');
        t.className = 'sim-line';
        terminal.append(t);
        decode(t, entry.text, { frames: 6, frameMs: 25 });
      }
      if (entry.layer === 'database') {
        seenDb++;
        if (seenDb === 1) {
          decode(queryLine, entry.text, { frames: 6, frameMs: 25 });
        } else if (seenDb === 2) {
          if (result.status === 200) {
            const user = result.body as { id: number; name: string; role: string };
            dbTable.hidden = false;
            dbEmpty.hidden = true;
            const tr = document.createElement('tr');
            for (const val of [user.id, user.name, user.role]) {
              const td = document.createElement('td');
              td.textContent = String(val);
              tr.append(td);
            }
            dbBody.append(tr);
          } else {
            dbTable.hidden = true;
            dbEmpty.hidden = false;
          }
        }
      }

      decode(textSpan, entry.text, { frames: 6, frameMs: 25, onDone: () => {
        i++;
        runTimer = window.setTimeout(step, 340);
      }});
    };
    step();
  }

  goBtn.addEventListener('click', () => run(input.value.trim() || '/api/users/1'));
  input.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
    if (e.key === 'Enter') { e.preventDefault(); run(input.value.trim() || '/api/users/1'); }
  });
  chips.forEach((chip) => chip.addEventListener('click', () => run(chip.dataset.path ?? '')));
</script>

<style>
  /* The whole page below the title breaks out of the article's 68ch
     reading column (see BaseLayout's .wrap) -- a Systems topic is meant
     to feel like the actual tool/environment it's teaching, not an
     article with a widget stapled in. Docs and the simulator share ONE
     bordered shell (not two separately-boxed sections) specifically so
     a taller docs column never reads as a layout bug next to a shorter
     main column -- there's no second box edge to look misaligned. */
  .workspace-page {
    position: relative; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%);
    width: 100vw; max-width: 92rem; box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 0 var(--sp-5);
    margin: var(--sp-5) 0 var(--sp-6);
  }
  .workspace-shell {
    border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg-1);
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 34rem 1fr;
  }
  @media (max-width: 60rem) {
    .workspace-shell { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .docs-panel { order: 2; position: static; border-right: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .workspace-main { order: 1; }
  }

  /* Docs blocks auto-flow into 2 columns once the sidebar is wide
     enough (desktop) -- with 8 blocks now, a single narrow column made
     this panel far taller than the simulator next to it, leaving a
     wide dead strip of empty shell background beside it. Two columns
     brings both sides' heights back in line with each other. */
  .docs-panel {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: var(--sp-3); align-content: start; position: sticky; top: var(--sp-4);
    padding: var(--sp-4); border-right: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .docs-block { border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg-0); padding: var(--sp-3); }
  .docs-label { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.64rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--accent); margin: 0 0 var(--sp-2); }
  .docs-block ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; display: grid; gap: var(--sp-2); font-size: 0.76rem; line-height: 1.4; color: var(--text-1); }
  .docs-block code { font-size: 0.9em; }
  .docs-block a { color: var(--accent); }

  /* container-type, not another viewport media query: the pipeline and
     tool-grid below need to react to *this column's actual rendered
     width*, which shrinks once the 34rem docs sidebar exists -- a
     viewport-width breakpoint doesn't know the sidebar ate that space,
     which is exactly what broke the pipeline diagram (Database wrapped
     alone onto its own row with a dangling arrow) at viewport widths
     just above the sidebar-stacking breakpoint. */
  .workspace-main { min-width: 0; container-type: inline-size; display: grid; gap: var(--sp-4); align-content: start; padding: var(--sp-4); }
  .workspace-toolbar { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: var(--sp-3); flex-wrap: wrap; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: var(--sp-3); }
  .workspace-title { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--step--1); font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); letter-spacing: 0.02em; }
  .workspace-hint { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.68rem; color: var(--text-2); }

  /* Aligns "Go deeper"/Related Topics to the same left/right edges as
     the workspace shell above -- otherwise the page narrows back to
     the article's 68ch width right under a much wider section, which
     reads as a layout mistake even though each piece is correct on
     its own. */
  .footer-page {
    position: relative; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%);
    width: 100vw; max-width: 92rem; box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 0 var(--sp-5);
  }
  /* Sources/RelatedTopics render one full-width row per item by default
     (tuned for the article's 68ch column) -- at this page's much wider
     footer that reads as stretched, so let them wrap into cards instead.
     Scoped by the .footer-page ancestor (only present on this page), so
     every other topic page keeps the unmodified single-column list. */
  .footer-page :global(.sources-list),
  .footer-page :global(.related-list) {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(18rem, 1fr));
  }

  /* pipeline diagram */
  .pipeline { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 0; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .pipe-node {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: var(--sp-1);
    padding: var(--sp-3); border: 1px solid var(--line-bright); background: var(--bg-0);
    min-width: 9rem; text-align: center;
  }
  .pipe-node.active { border-color: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--accent), 0 0 18px color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 40%, transparent); }
  .pipe-icon { font-size: var(--step-2); color: var(--text-1); }
  .pipe-node.active .pipe-icon { color: var(--accent); }
  .pipe-name { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-0); font-size: var(--step--1); letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .pipe-note { font-size: 0.68rem; color: var(--text-2); max-width: 9rem; }
  .pipe-edge { flex: 0 0 auto; width: 3rem; height: 2px; background: var(--line-bright); position: relative; }
  .pipe-edge::after { content: '▶'; position: absolute; right: -0.6rem; top: 50%; transform: translateY(-50%); font-size: 0.6rem; color: var(--line-bright); }
  .pipe-edge.active { background: var(--accent); }
  .pipe-edge.active::after { color: var(--accent); }
  .pipe-edge-note { position: absolute; top: -1.1rem; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); font-size: 0.6rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--text-2); white-space: nowrap; }
  @container (max-width: 40rem) {
    .pipeline { flex-direction: column; }
    .pipe-edge { width: 2px; height: 2rem; }
    .pipe-edge::after { content: '▼'; right: 50%; top: auto; bottom: -0.7rem; transform: translateX(50%); }
    .pipe-edge-note { top: 50%; left: -2rem; transform: translateY(-50%); }
  }

  /* controls */
  .addr-input-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--sp-2); flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .addr-proto { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--text-2); }
  .addr-input { flex: 1; min-width: 12rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.8rem; padding: var(--sp-2); background: var(--bg-0); border: 1px solid var(--line-bright); color: var(--text-0); }
  .addr-input:focus { outline: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .go-btn { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.8rem; padding: var(--sp-2) var(--sp-3); background: var(--accent); color: var(--bg-0); border: none; font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; }
  .go-btn:hover { background: var(--accent-deep); }
  .preset-chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--sp-2); }
  .chip { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.7rem; padding: var(--sp-1) var(--sp-2); background: var(--bg-0); border: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--text-1); cursor: pointer; }
  .chip:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--text-0); }

  /* tool windows */
  .tool-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--sp-3); }
  @container (max-width: 50rem) { .tool-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .tool-window { border: 1px solid var(--line-bright); background: var(--bg-0); display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-height: 17rem; }
  .tool-titlebar { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--sp-2); padding: var(--sp-2) var(--sp-3); background: var(--bg-1); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .tw-dots { display: flex; gap: 0.3rem; }
  .tw-dots i { width: 0.5rem; height: 0.5rem; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--line-bright); display: block; }
  .tw-tab { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.68rem; color: var(--text-2); }
  .tool-body { padding: var(--sp-3); flex: 1; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--sp-2); overflow: auto; }
  .net-log-label { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.62rem; color: var(--text-2); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin: 0; }

  .rendered-page { min-height: 5rem; border: 1px dashed var(--line); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: var(--sp-3); }
  .rp-placeholder, .rp-loading { color: var(--text-2); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; margin: 0; }
  .profile-card { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: var(--sp-1); }
  .avatar { width: 2.5rem; height: 2.5rem; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--bg-2); border: 1px solid var(--accent); color: var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 700; }
  .p-name { color: var(--text-0); font-weight: 700; }
